WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.767
Process Guide turns a video or live view into a guided workflow.

2
00:00:05.172 --> 00:00:11.501
Choose a video file, camera, or shared screen. Here, we use the parts sorting example.

3
00:00:11.906 --> 00:00:17.558
Upload a text guide, or choose a sample. Without a document, inferred steps remain provisional.

4
00:00:17.963 --> 00:00:23.328
Set your guidance preferences and personal wishes, then open the workspace.

5
00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:28.382
Your source stays on the left. Drag the divider to give either side more room.

6
00:00:28.787 --> 00:00:34.813
Steps and principles explain the action and its purpose. Evidence shows what the system observed.

7
00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:40.835
Review each result. Manual confirmations remain clearly separate from AI observations.

8
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:47.654
Ask a typed question, or use voice controls. Speech and microphone access require your action.

9
00:00:48.058 --> 00:00:53.022
Guardian adds ongoing observation. Pause guidance whenever you need to inspect the source.

10
00:00:53.427 --> 00:00:59.210
In Readiness, record the job context and complete your preparation checks before work.

11
00:00:59.615 --> 00:01:04.439
Review lets you bookmark a frame and raise an exception when evidence needs attention.

12
00:01:04.844 --> 00:01:10.257
Open the analysis report to review the workflow, observations, and unresolved issues.

13
00:01:10.662 --> 00:01:16.898
Prepare a PDF, export offline HTML, or share the file. Reports can include session details.

14
00:01:17.303 --> 00:01:21.711
Create or sign in to a private local account, then save the current result.

15
00:01:22.116 --> 00:01:29.715
Saved results remain available for review on this deployment. The simulator connection is planned, and inactive.
